A few possibilities:

* Sexually transmitted diseases cost time & money, can cause
  infertility or death (thus reducing number of present and
  future members).  For example, AIDs is taking a huge toll
  in Africa; any meme that can effectively stop AIDS-spreading
  behavior is being strongly selected for.  There may have
  been many such deadly STD outbreaks in the environs where
  Judaism, Christianity, Islam, etc. started and spread.
* Constant sexual activity, and romance in general, takes time 
  away from evangelism.  At the extreme we have monks, but
  they probably get more free time from not raising children
  than from not having sex.  Before good birth control, sex and
  children were inseparable; today dinks have nearly as much free
  memetic time as monks.
* Fathers tend to abandon or abuse children, divorce, etc. if they 
  think they have been cuckolded (this a consequence of "selfish gene" 
  or sociobiology theory).  Monogamy-teaching memes may thus promote
  intact families where the meme has the greatest chance
  of spreading to the next generation.

